s August to September came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years, the most of any pair. In 2025, January to February came in at 46% of normal and August to September at 51% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, April to May sat at 57% and June to July at 119% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 26025 had its driest year in 1964 at 63% of normal.</p>"}
